			<td class="BodyMain" width="88%" colspan="4" align="left"><font size="2">
			<h4 class="BodyMainH4">&nbsp;Who are the Armigers of Mirth?</h4>
			The Armigers of Mirth is a guild of avid MMORPG game fans initially formed in 
			an earlier incarnation in EverQuest<sup>©</sup> having now expanded beyond that<p>
			Some of us were ready to try some new MMORPGs, others still play EQ<sup>©</sup>, but we
			all share the love of the online games and envision the AofM as becoming
			a general guild for various MMORPGs.<p>
			In EQ<sup>©</sup> our common bond was lots of virtual drinking and brewing, we hope to be able to
			carry on a similiar tradition in AO<sup>©</sup> 
			<h4 class="BodyMainH4">&nbsp;What does &quot;Armigers of Mirth&quot; mean?</h4>
			<i>Armigers</i> comes from the Latin word meaning &quot;arms bearer&quot;, while <i>Mirth</i> comes from the
			old or middle English word meaning &quot;merriment and cheerfulness, often accompanied with laughter&quot;. 
			That tells you a lot about who we are...<p>
			<h4 class="BodyMainH4">&nbsp;So what do you do?</h4>
			Basically we enjoy playing onlines games with real life and online friends in
			a fun and co-operative setting. While games like Anarchy Online<sup>©</sup> have a PvP (Player vs. Player) element
			that may set up 'against' one another - we are a circle of friends who like sharing game information,
			helping our guild mates out, exploring the worlds we play in and having an all-around good time.<p>
			<h4 class="BodyMainH4">&nbsp;Whose side are you on in Anarchy Online<sup>©</sup>?</h4>
			Any. We don't exclude membership based on online persona, we play any profession and creed
			and any Allegiance. Our only allegiance per se, it to having good guildmates - people who
			play fairly and honestly, behaving respectfully towards other players, and don't do anything that
			would give the Guild or its members a bad reputation.  
			</font></td>
